    },
    {
      // no-runtime-typeof stays off ON PURPOSE in the two ops-scripts trees
      // below: a one-off probe of parsed JSON is not the unparsed-value
      // narrowing the rule exists to reject, and neither tree is typed product
      // code the rule exists to police. Repo-level scripts/ gates are NOT
      // covered — each honest boundary walk there carries its own per-site
      // disable with the reason, so deleting one surfaces as an unused
      // directive rather than silence.
      // oxlint-disarm: anti-slop/no-runtime-typeof — a one-off script's probe of parsed JSON is not the unparsed-value narrowing the rule rejects; ops tooling, not product seams.
      "files": ["apps/server/src/scripts/**", "packages/*/src/scripts/**"],
      "rules": {
        "anti-slop/no-runtime-typeof": "off"
      }
    },
    {
      // no-runtime-typeof stays off ON PURPOSE in the honest-boundary
      // files below. Each `typeof` there is the parse itself, a display or
      // redaction branch, or a typed-union discrimination with no helper
      // spelling — not an unparsed value narrowed in place of a boundary decode:
      // - canonical unknown-walkers and serializers (contracts guards,
      //   sanitize, bound, flatten-json, tools stringifyCanonical, web
      //   eden restoreWireTimestamps, signature canonicalize) dispatch on
      //   the runtime representation because the representation IS the
      //   contract being established;
      // - schema-boundary validators (contracts tool-schemas and
      //   tool-fields preprocessors, events z.custom, env server
      //   preprocessors, extraction protocol validators)
      //   narrow `unknown` process.env, webhook, and model-output fields
      //   inside the Zod boundary that owns them;
      // - provider and external-payload readers (fact-policy content
      //   probes) narrow webhook, provider, and persisted-JSON fields at
      //   the ingestion edge;
      // - unknown renderers (contracts text toDisplayText,
      //   metering captureInput,
      //   langfuse stripParams, logger error diagnostics,
      //   credential envelope open) branch
      //   `unknown` into text for display, logs, or redaction, which is
      //   the boundary;
      // - typed-union discriminators with no helper spelling (toast
      //   Shorthand, gateway RequestInfo, pipeline PropertyKey symbol arm,
      //   ReactNode discrimination in chat text renderers,
      //   auth credential-adapter seal walk over better-auth's loosely-typed
      //   adapter payloads) narrow an already-typed union whose arms differ
